# cbctl
`cbctl` is the Couchbase Server CLI for this project. Use it to provision and inspect clusters and keyspaces. Prefer invoking `cbctl` over ad-hoc REST or SDK scripts when the task matches a supported command.

Scope: Couchbase Server management (top-level commands) and Capella cloud management (`cbctl capella ...`, Capella Management API v4). Server commands never take Capella flags; Capella commands never take `--host`/`-u`/`-p`.

## Command map

# Cluster
cbctl cluster create --host 127.0.0.1 -u Administrator -p password --no-ssl
cbctl cluster create --name my-cluster --ip-address 10.0.0.1 --external-ip-address 203.0.113.10 --services data,index,query,fts --server-group us-east-1a --data-path /data/couchbase -p password --no-ssl
cbctl cluster join --rally-ip-address 10.0.0.1 --ip-address 10.0.0.2 --external-ip-address 203.0.113.11 --services data,index,query,fts --server-group us-east-1b --data-path /data/couchbase -p password --no-ssl
cbctl cluster add --rally-ip-address 10.0.0.1 --ip-address 10.0.0.2 -p password --no-ssl
cbctl cluster rebalance --rally-ip-address 10.0.0.1 -p password --no-ssl
cbctl cluster exists --host 127.0.0.1 -u Administrator -p password --no-ssl
cbctl cluster map --host 127.0.0.1 -u Administrator -p password --no-ssl
cbctl cluster test --host 127.0.0.1 -u Administrator -p password --no-ssl

